{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-250481",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={log}_{7}⁡(x+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={log}_{7}⁡(y+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={log}_{7}⁡(y+4) \\\\ {7}^{x} & ={7}^{{log}_{7}⁡(y+4)} \\\\ {7}^{x} & =y+4 \\\\ y & ={7}^{x}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is ${f}^{-1}(x)={7}^{x}-4.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
